# 90
#title feat: parse guide lines of a PR record in the app
#url https://github.com/MobileReality/lantern/pull/90
#branch feat/app-guide-parse
#base feat/guided-review
#opened 2026-11-26
#head 7b7248e4fc69a1c3e389fe51fc1de49172f6b6d7
#describe what The app reads the guide lines of a PR or branch record into a guide, or a guideError when they are malformed, exactly as the skill's guide parser does.
#describe before The app ignored guide lines in a record.
#describe after The record carries a guide with summary, risk and steps, or a guideError naming the first problem, and the rest of the record is untouched.
#describe verified Parity test, the full test suite and the typecheck are green.
#plan guided-pr-review s2.2
+ src/main/lantern-guide-parse.ts
+ test/helpers/lantern-guide-cases.ts
~ src/main/lantern-local.ts
~ src/main/lantern-pr-parse.ts
~ src/main/lantern-prs.ts
~ src/main/lantern-types.ts
~ test/lantern-pr-parity.test.ts
#order src/main/lantern-types.ts
#order src/main/lantern-guide-parse.ts
#order src/main/lantern-pr-parse.ts
#order src/main/lantern-prs.ts
#order src/main/lantern-local.ts
#order test/helpers/lantern-guide-cases.ts
#order test/lantern-pr-parity.test.ts
#reason src/main/lantern-guide-parse.ts Gives the app the same strict reading of guide lines as the skill, so a guide means one thing everywhere
#reason test/helpers/lantern-guide-cases.ts Holds the guide cases and their expected messages so the parity test stays short
#reason src/main/lantern-local.ts Carries the guide of a local branch record onto its comparison like the flow
#reason src/main/lantern-pr-parse.ts Collects the guide lines of a record and keeps a bad guide from breaking the rest of it
#reason src/main/lantern-prs.ts Carries the parsed guide from a PR record onto the PR the map shows
#reason src/main/lantern-types.ts Defines the guide shape the review screen will read, with guideError beside it like flowError
#reason test/lantern-pr-parity.test.ts Fails when the app and the skill read a guide differently or the mirrored limits drift
#story A reviewer opens a PR that carries a guide
#step actor A reviewer
#step action opens a pull request record with guide lines in
#file src/main/lantern-pr-parse.ts
#file src/main/lantern-prs.ts
#step subject Lantern
#below actor Lantern
#below interaction can now read the guide steps of the PR
#file src/main/lantern-guide-parse.ts
#file test/lantern-pr-parity.test.ts
#below consequence guide lines were ignored => guide steps are read and checked
#file src/main/lantern-types.ts
#story A malformed guide does not hide the PR
#step actor A reviewer
#step action opens a record whose guide is malformed in
#file test/helpers/lantern-guide-cases.ts
#step subject Lantern
#below actor Lantern
#below interaction still shows the PR and says why the guide failed
#below consequence no word on a bad guide => the first problem is named
